(7503402, 1195799, 2333, '<td valign="top">You obviously had a lot of moonlight! I really would like to see more stars, but with that much moonlight you are limited as to what you can get. Timing with a low lunar % illumination would be necessary to get the right balance of starry sky and illumination of the land. It''s possible under starlight only (new moon), but you need a *lot* of exposure time.</td>', 'You obviously had a lot of moonlight! I really would like to see more stars, but with that much moonlight you are limited as to what you can get. Timing with a low lunar % illumination would be necessary to get the right balance of starry sky and illumination of the land. It''s possible under starlight only (new moon), but you need a *lot* of exposure time.', '2017-03-03 09:41:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503403, 1195837, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A very calm and tranquil scene that would soothe anyone in the room in which it was hanging. The blue of the sea is a nice contrast against that of the variegated sky. The composition is good with the sky very clearly emphasised. If Im really pedantic, which is what Im here for folks, there are a couple of minor issues. First their appears to be faint banding in the sky, most noticeable in the mid blues. And secondly the horizon has a very slight tilt to the left. They both have to be looked for very hard so they are not detrimental to the image.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A very calm and tranquil scene that would soothe anyone in the room in which it was hanging. The blue of the sea is a nice contrast against that of the variegated sky. The composition is good with the sky very clearly emphasised. If Im really pedantic, which is what Im here for folks, there are a couple of minor issues. First their appears to be faint banding in the sky, most noticeable in the mid blues. And secondly the horizon has a very slight tilt to the left. They both have to be looked for very hard so they are not detrimental to the image.', '2017-03-03 09:47:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503404, 1195817, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Im sorry Janine but I have to agree with Mike here, given the nature of the challenge, in my mind this is a long way from minimalist. You have found an appealing landscape and stamped your usual authority on it, there are no problems technically although the blues feel a little too strong they could do with pulling back a little. Obviously I dont know what the rest of your scene was like but if you could have taken this from further away with the buildings much more insignificant then I think this would have come nearer to the challenge brief but even then that sky is very busy. The small galvanised shed on its own in the distance as a focal point would be much nearer to my idea of minimalist.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that does not meet the challenge Im sorry Janine but I have to agree with Mike here, given the nature of the challenge, in my mind this is a long way from minimalist. You have found an appealing landscape and stamped your usual authority on it, there are no problems technically although the blues feel a little too strong they could do with pulling back a little. Obviously I dont know what the rest of your scene was like but if you could have taken this from further away with the buildings much more insignificant then I think this would have come nearer to the challenge brief but even then that sky is very busy. The small galvanised shed on its own in the distance as a focal point would be much nearer to my idea of minimalist.', '2017-03-03 09:56:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503407, 1195799, 109387, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kirbic:</b></div><hr/><i> You obviously had a lot of moonlight! I really would like to see more stars, but with that much moonlight you are limited as to what you can get. Timing with a low lunar % illumination would be necessary to get the right balance of starry sky and illumination of the land. It''s possible under starlight only (new moon), but you need a *lot* of exposure time. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Fritz thanks for your comment. We had almost full moon. It''s impossible to take videos in pitch black conditions and my friend/colleague Fortunato (several times awarded in the most important nature contests in the world) loves to take images during moonlit nights. Even with a super ISO monster like A7SII you need moon in the sky. In this case I was shooting time-lapse and this one was the sequence I shot before taking the photo:<br/> <br/><a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BweBOjAmRBm5WUVVbThXTGpRVWc/view?usp=sharing" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Moon</a></td>', 'Originally posted by kirbic: You obviously had a lot of moonlight! I really would like to see more stars, but with that much moonlight you are limited as to what you can get. Timing with a low lunar % illumination would be necessary to get the right balance of starry sky and illumination of the land. It''s possible under starlight only (new moon), but you need a *lot* of exposure time.   Fritz thanks for your comment. We had almost full moon. It''s impossible to take videos in pitch black conditions and my friend/colleague Fortunato (several times awarded in the most important nature contests in the world) loves to take images during moonlit nights. Even with a super ISO monster like A7SII you need moon in the sky. In this case I was shooting time-lapse and this one was the sequence I shot before taking the photo: Moon', '2017-03-03 10:01:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503408, 1195271, 25024, '<td valign="top">Well done Marcel. A perfect representation of the challenge brief. Wow, look at those ribbons lining up, star pupil...</td>', 'Well done Marcel. A perfect representation of the challenge brief. Wow, look at those ribbons lining up, star pupil...', '2017-03-03 10:01:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7503413, 1195670, 167587, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by giantmike:</b></div><hr/><i> Sure is hard to make the brown dead field look good, isn''t it? Maybe try adding a bit of green in processing to see if that helps. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Funny, I wasn''t bothered by the brown, dead field. Actually, I liked it and believe that it adds to the "minimalist" concept in the challenge. No need to make it "look good."  Thanks for your thoughts and comment.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by giantmike: Sure is hard to make the brown dead field look good, isn''t it? Maybe try adding a bit of green in processing to see if that helps.   Funny, I wasn''t bothered by the brown, dead field. Actually, I liked it and believe that it adds to the "minimalist" concept in the challenge. No need to make it "look good."  Thanks for your thoughts and comment.', '2017-03-03 10:30:32.000000', NULL, 0),
