(7504152, 1195776, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by giantmike:</b></div><hr/><i> One thing to watch out for with wide angle lenses is distortion at the edges. IF you fixed the distortion of this in post processing, I bet it would look cleaner and nicer. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>But you see, I LIKE the way it looks like this.  It''s like the trees are teammates and huddling toward each other.  LOL<br/> <br/>Actually, I don''t really see much in the way of distortion.  Where do you see it?  If there''s distortion, how could the trees in the background show vertical trunks (or nearly vertical anyway)?</td>', 'Originally posted by giantmike: One thing to watch out for with wide angle lenses is distortion at the edges. IF you fixed the distortion of this in post processing, I bet it would look cleaner and nicer.  But you see, I LIKE the way it looks like this.  It''s like the trees are teammates and huddling toward each other.  LOL Actually, I don''t really see much in the way of distortion.  Where do you see it?  If there''s distortion, how could the trees in the background show vertical trunks (or nearly vertical anyway)?', '2017-03-06 20:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
